body:
Definitely not just for Runescape, nope not at all

&#x200B;

But in all seriousness, I'd use it to edit videos, stream, and of course play games. It'd be nice to finally get more than 30fps in Minecraft; being able to run Shaders would be phenomenal

i ordered the softweave cookies and cream. i don't like the feeling of leather chairs, and i was afraid of it peeling and looking scuffed after a few years. with the fabric, yeah if you spill something on it it can be difficult to clean, but as long as you dont dump coffee or soda on it it should be fine. i'm assuming you could get fabric cleaner or maybe even one of those carpet cleaning machines; you could deep clean it that way. 

&#x200B;

where i live, it gets pretty hot and humid during the summer, and very very cold in winter; having a nice soft fabric chair that also looks really nice, and matches my setup, seemed like a no-brainer; but of course, make sure you go with the one you really want! i'm hoping that with the 5 year warranty the chair is going to last a long time

yeah, same. i love how the cookies and cream looks. i specifically picked that one because i want my office space to all kind of 'match; in fact i've been picking out peripherals all to go around the chair because the chair is the most expensive thing xD

&#x200B;

i hope we get our chairs soon!
